1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,643
In this town, you only get one hundred words per day.

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:07,231
Everyone has a counter on their chest.

3
00:00:08,027 --> 00:00:10,398
Every word you say, it goes down.

4
00:00:11,193 --> 00:00:14,474
When it hits zero, your voice is gone until tomorrow.

5
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,325
So nobody wastes words here.

6
00:00:17,893 --> 00:00:19,052
No small talk.

7
00:00:19,693 --> 00:00:21,155
No "how are you."

8
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:22,483
Just nods.

9
00:00:23,427 --> 00:00:26,404
My little sister Pia spends her words on singing.

10
00:00:27,393 --> 00:00:29,765
Every morning. All one hundred of them.

11
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,537
Then she's quiet for the rest of the day.

12
00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:36,292
Dad says she's wasting them.

13
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:39,837
Pia says songs are the only words worth saying.

14
00:00:40,827 --> 00:00:43,198
Then the mayor announced a new rule.

15
00:00:43,993 --> 00:00:45,455
Words don't reset anymore.

16
00:00:45,927 --> 00:00:48,904
Whatever you have left... is all you'll ever get.

17
00:00:49,893 --> 00:00:51,658
The whole town went silent.

18
00:00:52,227 --> 00:00:53,689
People started hoarding words.

19
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:55,016
Selling them.

20
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:56,816
Stealing them.

21
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,222
I had forty-two left.

22
00:00:59,693 --> 00:01:00,852
Pia had zero.

23
00:01:01,493 --> 00:01:03,562
She had already sung that morning.

24
00:01:04,227 --> 00:01:05,992
She would never speak again.

25
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,931
She just looked at me and smiled.

26
00:01:09,727 --> 00:01:12,098
That night, I found the mayor's office.

27
00:01:12,893 --> 00:01:14,052
A giant machine.

28
00:01:14,693 --> 00:01:15,852
Full of words.

29
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:17,652
Millions of them.

30
00:01:18,293 --> 00:01:19,149
Everyone's words.

31
00:01:20,093 --> 00:01:21,555
He wasn't saving them.

32
00:01:22,027 --> 00:01:23,489
He was collecting them.

33
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,422
For one giant speech.

34
00:01:25,893 --> 00:01:29,174
One that would make everyone in town obey him forever.

35
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:31,722
I had forty-two words.

36
00:01:32,193 --> 00:01:33,655
I needed exactly one.

37
00:01:34,127 --> 00:01:35,589
I pressed the microphone.

38
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:37,219
And I sang.

39
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:39,019
The machine cracked.

40
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:41,425
Words flew out like birds.

41
00:01:41,993 --> 00:01:43,152
Back to everyone.

42
00:01:43,793 --> 00:01:45,255
Pia opened her mouth.

43
00:01:45,727 --> 00:01:48,098
And she sang the whole morning song.

44
00:01:48,893 --> 00:01:50,658
My counter says zero now.

45
00:01:51,227 --> 00:01:52,386
I don't mind.

46
00:01:53,027 --> 00:01:55,398
She talks enough for both of us.

